  "generated_text": "We recognize that $\\mathbf{A}$ is a rotation matrix by $\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ radians around the $z$-axis. Thus, $\\mathbf{A}^{2018}$ is a rotation matrix by $\\frac{\\pi}{6} \\cdot 2018 = 338\\pi$ radians around the $z$-axis.\n\nSince $338\\pi$ is a multiple of $2\\pi$, we can reduce the angle modulo $2\\pi$:\n\\[ 338\\pi \\equiv 2\\pi \\pmod{2\\pi}. \\]\n\nTherefore, $\\mathbf{A}^{2018}$ is a rotation matrix by $2\\pi$ radians around the $z$-axis, which is equivalent to a rotation by $360^\\circ$ radians.\n\nThe rotation matrix by $360^\\circ$ around the $z$-axis is the identity matrix:\n\\[ \\mathbf{A}^{2018} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\end{pmatrix}. \\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\\boxed{\\mathbf{I}}.\\]",
